{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01ML4ELhmET3QSnDefHuBUr4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Wrote **`answers/06-010-why-neural-networks-not-first-choice-for-tabular-data.md`** covering:\n\n- **Concept:** GBTs encode inductive biases that match tabular structure; NNs learn representations from scratch with no architectural advantage when features are already hand-engineered.\n- **5 structural reasons:** sample efficiency gap (10K–500K rows typical), heterogeneous feature handling, no spatial/sequential structure, regularization complexity, TreeSHAP interpretability.\n- **When NNs do win:** millions of rows, multimodal fusion (DeepFM, two-tower), high-cardinality entity embeddings.\n- **Benchmark anchor:** Grinsztajn et al. NeurIPS 2022 — GBTs outperformed tabular DL on 60%+ of 45 datasets.\n- **Production example:** credit-risk scoring — XGBoost AUC 0.87 in 3 min vs 5-layer MLP AUC 0.84 in 45 min, with TreeSHAP feeding directly into compliance reports.\n\nNext up: **Q11 — Imbalanced datasets in real projects?**"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":283,"cache_read_input_tokens":69732,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":283,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b1a98872-b77f-44c5-bd0e-42f5a1909969","uuid":"b4c51df3-a8b3-432f-b38b-eef97909b71d"}
